WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.209 --> 00:00:07.003
I want to invite you
over for dinner at my house.

00:00:08.046 --> 00:00:09.631
When you walk in,

00:00:09.673 --> 00:00:11.758
there are chairs cramped everywhere,

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.968
smells delicious,

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:14.678
you hear people laughing,

00:00:14.678 --> 00:00:17.222
you see friends hugging
and telling stories.

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:20.308
There are more than 20 of us here tonight.

00:00:20.642 --> 00:00:24.354
Teachers, tech leaders, lawyers, moms.

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:28.024
It’s loud, and it’s chaotic.

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:31.653
But even if this is your first time,

00:00:31.653 --> 00:00:33.196
it feels like home.

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:36.825
And then we'll sit down to work.

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:39.536
Because tonight is not a regular dinner.

00:00:39.869 --> 00:00:43.206
Tonight is the culmination
of months of conversations

00:00:43.248 --> 00:00:44.749
and learning in my living room.

00:00:45.792 --> 00:00:47.627
At the end of this night,

00:00:47.669 --> 00:00:51.840
30,000 dollars will go out
to a local grassroots nonprofit

00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:54.884
that is doing amazing work
in our community.

00:00:56.011 --> 00:01:00.015
And that money came
from everyone in the room.

00:01:00.682 --> 00:01:04.102
And the decision of where
that money is going

00:01:04.144 --> 00:01:06.438
included all of our voices.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:11.067
This is a giving circle:

00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:13.278
a group of people with shared values

00:01:13.278 --> 00:01:15.614
that comes together to create change.

00:01:17.282 --> 00:01:18.825
My giving circle,

00:01:18.867 --> 00:01:20.577
the Peninsula Latina Giving Circle,

00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:22.912
is what I know philanthropy to be.

00:01:23.455 --> 00:01:24.706
It's joyful.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.334
And transformative

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.836
and collaborative and intentional.

00:01:30.837 --> 00:01:34.090
Most people don't see us
as philanthropists

00:01:34.132 --> 00:01:35.717
or this process

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:37.677
when they think of philanthropy.

00:01:37.677 --> 00:01:40.639
But I'm here to show you
the powerful possibility

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.975
that exists in all of us
to be philanthropists,

00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:46.478
no matter your age or your wealth,

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:48.897
no matter where you live
or where you come from.

00:01:49.898 --> 00:01:52.692
I am originally from Mexico City,

00:01:52.692 --> 00:01:55.445
moved to the US 25 years ago,

00:01:55.487 --> 00:01:59.574
and in 2007, when I started
my first giving circle,

00:01:59.616 --> 00:02:02.202
I didn't even know the concept had a name.

00:02:02.243 --> 00:02:03.495
This is not new.

00:02:03.953 --> 00:02:06.831
Collective giving has been
going on for centuries.

00:02:07.165 --> 00:02:09.459
Just in the past two decades,

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:13.213
thousands of giving circles
got started all over the world,

00:02:13.254 --> 00:02:16.508
collectively giving more
than 1.3 billion dollars.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.345
(Applause)

00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:22.972
I have dedicated my life to this work.

00:02:23.473 --> 00:02:26.893
And now I lead an organization
called Philanthropy Together

00:02:26.935 --> 00:02:30.980
to democratize and diversify
the power of philanthropy

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.274
through the power of giving circles.

00:02:34.526 --> 00:02:38.196
There are giving circles
with five members or 500,

00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:42.117
each person giving
five dollars or 250,000,

00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:45.995
iIncluding any generation,
identity or geography.

00:02:46.621 --> 00:02:48.623
We give to nonprofits,

00:02:48.623 --> 00:02:50.083
we give to individuals

00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:52.627
or to new projects
just getting off the ground.

00:02:53.378 --> 00:02:55.463
There are women's giving circles

00:02:55.505 --> 00:02:57.340
and Black giving circles,

00:02:57.382 --> 00:03:00.427
Jewish, Muslim and interfaith.

00:03:00.885 --> 00:03:03.221
Giving circles that focus
on climate change

00:03:03.263 --> 00:03:04.806
and civic engagement.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.892
Cross-class and cross-race
giving circles.

00:03:08.518 --> 00:03:12.814
Asian Pacific Islanders and Latinx LGBTQ.

00:03:12.856 --> 00:03:14.983
Giving circles inside companies.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:18.737
And social clubs and virtual.

00:03:18.778 --> 00:03:21.156
There are giving circles in Malawi

00:03:21.156 --> 00:03:23.575
and China and Germany.

00:03:23.575 --> 00:03:28.705
So these groups keep
getting together year over year

00:03:28.705 --> 00:03:31.708
because collective giving is powerful.

00:03:32.292 --> 00:03:37.547
We can have a much bigger impact
together than we can alone.

00:03:38.548 --> 00:03:41.009
So what is the secret?

00:03:41.843 --> 00:03:46.306
I'm here to show you the four steps
to start a thriving giving circle.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:49.934
The first step is to create belonging.

00:03:50.435 --> 00:03:53.730
The concept of people
banding together to create change

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.316
is as old as humanity itself.

00:03:57.484 --> 00:04:01.362
And collective giving has roots
in cultures all around the world.

00:04:02.322 --> 00:04:05.784
But today we don't even talk
to our neighbors anymore.

00:04:06.743 --> 00:04:10.497
But by belonging to something
that is bigger than ourselves

00:04:10.497 --> 00:04:14.209
and the collective power
of our dreams and voices,

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:20.298
that is what creates that lasting
commitment to each other and to change.

00:04:21.216 --> 00:04:23.551
Now [with] giving circles,
you start with a group.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.805
Friends, neighbors, colleagues.

00:04:27.305 --> 00:04:30.892
And you take the time
to deepen those relationships.

00:04:31.643 --> 00:04:36.397
Those folks back in my living room,
we basically started as strangers.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:41.611
But because we ate together
and laughed together and shared stories

00:04:41.611 --> 00:04:45.281
and decided on our shared set of values,

00:04:45.281 --> 00:04:49.327
we ended up creating a lasting community

00:04:49.327 --> 00:04:52.288
that gets together year over year.

00:04:52.997 --> 00:04:55.500
Giving circles make you feel at home.

00:04:56.751 --> 00:05:00.880
The second step is to hold
space for discourse.

00:05:01.256 --> 00:05:04.133
It can be completely,
completely overwhelming

00:05:04.175 --> 00:05:06.845
to know how to make
an impact as an individual.

00:05:06.845 --> 00:05:08.388
But in a giving circle,

00:05:08.429 --> 00:05:10.807
you have the opportunity
to learn together.

00:05:11.641 --> 00:05:16.187
Dozens of people engaging
in challenging conversations,

00:05:16.187 --> 00:05:19.732
getting new perspectives
about the issues in their communities.

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:25.864
We work across differences
and ideologies and viewpoints.

00:05:25.905 --> 00:05:29.158
But because everyone has an equal voice,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.704
we always walk in with something to share

00:05:32.745 --> 00:05:35.248
and walk away with something learned.

00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:38.126
And back in my living room,

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.128
we’re tackling the hardest part:

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.965
to decide where are we giving together.

00:05:44.966 --> 00:05:48.303
So we'll learn and then we'll vote,

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:51.055
and we'll discuss,
and we'll change our minds.

00:05:51.097 --> 00:05:53.308
And then we'll change our minds again.

00:05:54.058 --> 00:05:55.977
But beyond fail,

00:05:55.977 --> 00:05:58.938
we always come to an agreement at the end

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.190
because we come with an open heart

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.567
and an open mind.

00:06:03.109 --> 00:06:04.694
Now giving circle,

00:06:04.736 --> 00:06:06.988
is not about me or you.

00:06:07.614 --> 00:06:10.116
It's about us together.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:15.038
And once we have shared and discussed,

00:06:15.038 --> 00:06:18.291
the third step is to give with trust.

00:06:19.417 --> 00:06:21.210
Because in a giving circle,

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.088
we give altogether
to a shared pot of funding

00:06:24.088 --> 00:06:28.301
before even knowing
where that money is going to go.

00:06:29.052 --> 00:06:30.428
We trust each other,

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.307
and that trust extends
to the groups that we're funding.

00:06:35.808 --> 00:06:39.562
Tonight we're deciding
to give to a small nonprofit

00:06:39.604 --> 00:06:41.481
with a tiny, tiny budget.

00:06:42.607 --> 00:06:44.484
These numbers may shock you,

00:06:44.525 --> 00:06:46.277
but in the US,

00:06:46.319 --> 00:06:48.404
88 percent of funding

00:06:48.446 --> 00:06:51.991
goes to just the top five
percent of nonprofits.

00:06:53.618 --> 00:06:56.871
And groups led by Black and Latino leaders

00:06:56.913 --> 00:07:02.001
get far less funding than similar groups
led by white leaders.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.130
My giving circle,

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:09.342
we give as you would to a loved one,

00:07:09.342 --> 00:07:11.052
looking them in the eyes.

00:07:12.387 --> 00:07:15.098
And unlike most
of traditional philanthropy,

00:07:15.139 --> 00:07:17.850
we give with no strings attached,

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.645
literally shifting the power

00:07:20.645 --> 00:07:23.606
into the hands
of the leaders on the ground,

00:07:23.648 --> 00:07:27.026
so they can decide
how to best use the money.

00:07:27.902 --> 00:07:31.698
(Applause)

00:07:31.698 --> 00:07:35.118
Because community knows
what community needs.

00:07:35.118 --> 00:07:37.245
For any philanthropist,

00:07:37.286 --> 00:07:41.082
it should never be about parachuting
into a community to “save” it.

00:07:41.791 --> 00:07:44.711
Just acting alongside in partnership.

00:07:45.586 --> 00:07:47.296
They don't need to be saved.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.298
They need to be trusted.

00:07:50.299 --> 00:07:52.844
(Applause)

00:07:52.885 --> 00:07:56.973
And the last step
is just to act in abundance.

00:07:58.141 --> 00:08:00.768
When people think of philanthropy,

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.271
they usually just think of big money.

00:08:04.105 --> 00:08:05.273
And of course, you know,

00:08:05.314 --> 00:08:07.984
money is a big part
of a giving circle, too.

00:08:08.484 --> 00:08:10.278
Because of the multiplying effect,

00:08:10.319 --> 00:08:14.574
my 100 dollars can turn
into 10,000 or 100,000.

00:08:17.493 --> 00:08:22.290
You know, I even can make my kids look
outside of their phones for two minutes

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:26.127
and pay attention when I'm telling them
that I just gave 50,000 dollars.

00:08:27.045 --> 00:08:32.091
But philanthropy literally
is love of humanity.

00:08:32.925 --> 00:08:35.887
Giving with an abundance
of heart and of spirit.

00:08:36.387 --> 00:08:41.768
We can all be radically generous
in so many ways,

00:08:41.768 --> 00:08:43.227
beyond just money.

00:08:45.104 --> 00:08:46.898
So after tonight,

00:08:46.939 --> 00:08:51.569
we all are going to go
and volunteer and advocate

00:08:51.611 --> 00:08:54.405
and open doors and share in social media.

00:08:55.281 --> 00:08:58.493
We call this, in giving circles,
giving your five Ts:

00:08:59.535 --> 00:09:00.870
time,

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.163
talent,

00:09:02.205 --> 00:09:03.539
treasure,

00:09:03.581 --> 00:09:04.749
testimony

00:09:04.791 --> 00:09:05.917
and ties.

00:09:08.836 --> 00:09:12.215
One of my favorite stories of abundance

00:09:12.215 --> 00:09:14.217
is that of Martin Vargas Vega.

00:09:15.384 --> 00:09:20.181
The son of migrant farm workers
whose dream was to become a coder.

00:09:21.641 --> 00:09:27.313
Martin got trained by a small tech-skills
nonprofit in his community.

00:09:29.065 --> 00:09:32.693
That nonprofit was supported
by the Latinos in Tech Giving Circle.

00:09:33.194 --> 00:09:38.074
And for Martin, it was incredibly powerful
to see a group of people

00:09:38.074 --> 00:09:40.076
that looked like him,

00:09:40.118 --> 00:09:43.412
supporting and fueling the work
of the nonprofit

00:09:43.454 --> 00:09:44.789
that was training him.

00:09:45.706 --> 00:09:48.626
So after his training,

00:09:48.626 --> 00:09:53.714
Martin landed this high-profile
internship in Silicon Valley.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.968
And the very first thing he did

00:09:57.009 --> 00:09:59.470
was give 50 percent,

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:03.057
half of his signing bonus,
to that nonprofit.

00:10:04.016 --> 00:10:06.602
(Applause)

00:10:06.602 --> 00:10:07.854
And wait.

00:10:08.563 --> 00:10:11.065
And the other half

00:10:11.107 --> 00:10:13.651
to join the Latinos in Tech Giving Circle,

00:10:13.651 --> 00:10:16.195
because he is a philanthropist.

00:10:16.863 --> 00:10:19.574
Martin is -- thank you.

00:10:19.615 --> 00:10:24.245
Martin is actively using
his voice and his power

00:10:24.287 --> 00:10:28.082
to bring more STEM programs
for kids that look like him.

00:10:28.499 --> 00:10:30.626
That is abundance.

00:10:31.836 --> 00:10:34.255
Life changing things happen

00:10:34.297 --> 00:10:37.133
when we look at philanthropy
beyond the money,

00:10:37.133 --> 00:10:41.095
because all the money in the world
is not going to save us.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.681
But beloved communities will.

00:10:47.018 --> 00:10:48.895
For a long time,

00:10:48.895 --> 00:10:51.647
philanthropy has been just a select few

00:10:52.356 --> 00:10:55.860
... that decide
on the impact on many

00:10:55.902 --> 00:10:57.945
who should and shouldn't get funding,

00:10:57.987 --> 00:11:00.865
what is and what is not
considered impactful.

00:11:01.991 --> 00:11:03.993
Again, in the US,

00:11:04.035 --> 00:11:07.747
communities of color
receive eight percent of philanthropy.

00:11:08.956 --> 00:11:11.209
For women and girl's issues,

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:14.712
it's just 1.9 percent.

00:11:16.923 --> 00:11:22.720
Not even one third of one percent

00:11:22.762 --> 00:11:24.805
goes to the LGBTQ community.

00:11:26.474 --> 00:11:28.392
We have to change that.

00:11:29.518 --> 00:11:35.066
When we shift the power of philanthropy
into all of our voices,

00:11:35.066 --> 00:11:37.652
we change who gives,

00:11:37.693 --> 00:11:39.237
how we give,

00:11:39.237 --> 00:11:41.697
and ultimately, what gets funded.

00:11:43.491 --> 00:11:47.787
Giving by, for and with
the communities we represent

00:11:47.828 --> 00:11:49.622
is the future of philanthropy.

00:11:49.664 --> 00:11:52.959
And each and every one of us

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.669
belong in this movement.

00:11:56.254 --> 00:11:59.507
(Applause)

00:11:59.548 --> 00:12:01.676
Just think.

00:12:02.134 --> 00:12:05.888
What if every town, every issue,

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.015
every community

00:12:08.057 --> 00:12:11.894
had a giving circle with passionate
philanthropists like you?

00:12:14.355 --> 00:12:19.402
So if you're looking
for impact and connection

00:12:19.402 --> 00:12:21.445
and purpose

00:12:21.487 --> 00:12:23.531
and joy,

00:12:23.531 --> 00:12:26.242
join or start a giving circle,

00:12:26.242 --> 00:12:30.079
no matter if you have
five dollars to give or 50 million.

00:12:30.663 --> 00:12:33.291
No matter if you are a teacher

00:12:33.291 --> 00:12:36.419
or a tech leader or a lawyer or a mom.

00:12:38.713 --> 00:12:41.382
And if you do have millions

00:12:41.424 --> 00:12:43.634
or billions to give,

00:12:43.676 --> 00:12:45.386
join us in this movement.

00:12:46.012 --> 00:12:50.308
Match a hundredfold or invest
alongside a local giving circle.

00:12:53.311 --> 00:12:56.022
Thank you so much for coming
to my giving circle tonight.

00:12:57.732 --> 00:13:00.359
In a world that feels heavy,

00:13:00.401 --> 00:13:05.614
doing philanthropy together fills me
with so much joy and hope for the future.

00:13:07.366 --> 00:13:09.994
Maybe when we started

00:13:09.994 --> 00:13:12.496
you thought you were only
coming for dinner.

00:13:13.414 --> 00:13:17.251
But actually, you just got
an invitation to change a world.

00:13:18.502 --> 00:13:20.504
Let's meet at your house next time.

00:13:21.088 --> 00:13:22.256
(Spanish) Gracias.

00:13:22.298 --> 00:13:27.345
(Applause and cheers)

